# No commit — handoff / Cursor prompt delivery docs

## Rule

**Do not commit** backend/frontend handoff notes or Cursor prompt delivery documents into this monorepo.

These files are temporary delivery artifacts for BE/FE agents. They are not durable frontend SSOT.

## Filename patterns (non-exhaustive)

Treat paths matching any of the following (case-insensitive) as delivery docs:

- `*backend-request*`
- `*backend-prompt*`
- `*backend-cursor-prompt*`
- `*backend-handoff*`
- `*frontend-handoff*`
- `*cursor-prompt*`
- `*handoff*` when the file is a one-off API/seed delivery note under `**/docs/api/**`

Typical locations:

- `apps/cms/docs/api/**`
- `apps/admin/docs/api/**`
- `apps/platform/docs/api/**`

## Exceptions (keep)

Do **not** delete or block these:

- `*.json` seed / payload assets (e.g. `*.payload.json`, `*.db-rows.json`)
- Durable FE contracts and guides: `*-api-integration.md`, `*-api-migration-guide.md`, `*-fe-adapter*`, `*-fe-acceptance*`, `orval-codegen.md`, `api-routes-and-client.md`, form-template contract/SSOT docs
- Cursor rules / skills under `.cursor/rules/**` and `**/.cursor/rules/**` (this policy applies to delivery markdown under `docs/`, not rules themselves)
- Audit extracts under `docs/audit/**` only when the user explicitly asks to keep an audit report

## At commit time

Before creating a git commit:

1. Scan the staging area and working tree for delivery docs matching the patterns above.
2. If any remain, **delete them** (or unstage and delete) instead of committing them.
3. Do not use `--no-verify` to bypass this cleanup.
4. Prefer regenerating a prompt in chat or leaving it only in the BE repo / external handoff channel—not in the frontend git history.

## Intent

Frontend git should keep integration guides, seed **JSON**, and living FE contracts—not piles of “Cursor prompt — tell JABACK to …” markdown once the work is delivered.
